+## Adapter entry points and concrete blockers
+
+See `benchmarks/energy/REPRODUCE.md` for complete later-only interfaces/examples.
+
+- **T:** `beam_tools.py run/campaign`, `engine_options`, `slo_controls`: explicit
+  binary/package/root pins; A/B/B2/B3/C/D/S2 mode mapping, config budgets/SLOs,
+  local server lifecycle, ordered case lists. Original shell scripts are **not**
+  unchanged-runnable: hardcoded workspace paths, global GPU mutations and old
+  control interfaces are adapted. The separate opt-in same-TP/asymmetric-PP P2P
+  implementation is documented in `BEAM_P2P_COMPATIBILITY.md` (read-only here),
+  including its asymmetric-TP rejection and transport/layout limits. `pipeline` sequences typed tool
+  commands, including generation, fresh Dynamo sweeps, evaluation and plots.
+  Target validation accepts descendant stage commits and records actual port
+  SHA/dirty metadata. B clocks now run only in assigned workers via the native
+  worker-extension and authenticated dev-RPC middleware; no driver NVML exists.
+  The private token lives only in unregistered BEAM_TOOLS_RPC_TOKEN; inherited
+  native/client API-key variables are removed from the server child. Whole-server
+  HTTP/websocket authentication covers dev mutations as well as inference/SLOs;
+  only exact GET health and HTTP OPTIONS are public.
+  Typed POST chunk/microbatch and GET status clients retain acknowledgments and
+  poll every engine until effective state or timeout. Harness scalar/clear/
+  pattern controls are opt-in; pending/superseded m is never reported as applied.
+- **R:** `benchmark_script.py load_trace/synthetic/replay/metrics` and
+  `backend_request_func.py request/consume_sse`: complete timestamp CSV replay,
+  weighted gamma burst/stair workloads, OpenAI completion/chat HTTP and fidelity
+  snapshots, seconds/raw arrays plus millisecond metrics, failures/goodput.
+  Native delta token IDs identify even empty-decoded terminal tokens; grouped
+  token counts remain separate from chunk counts and text fallback is marked
+  unknown. Synthetic rate panels use explicit phase ends and step coordinates.
+  Other serving backends and multimodal datasets are explicitly unported.
+- **P:** `beam_tools.py offline-profile/profile_generation/summarize_profile`:
+  actual generation; worker profile starts before repeated forwards and stops
+  afterward; warmup excluded; rank-local final-stop counter deltas, not enqueue
+  energy attribution. `mixed-profile` now consumes the actual owned native
+  `EngineCore.beam_profile_trial` via SyncMP core utility or direct Inproc owner,
+  never worker collective RPC. It measures exact requested/observed coordinates,
+  skips mismatches, validates rank CSV scheduled work and exports separate
+  window-energy tables/aggregates. Schema `beam_owned_mixed_window_v1` remains
+  `legacy_lookup_compatible=false`, `calibration_claim=false`: numerical-domain
+  review/recalibration is not a missing API blocker. `generation-grid` also supplies
+  actual-request tables across batch/input/output/clock points, with completed
+  point resume guarded by post-cleanup completion markers, table/manifest hashes,
+  schema/clock×rank coverage, source/artifact fingerprints and consistent UUID maps.
+  Tables/final grids publish atomically, and an existing final grid is verified.
+  Idle physical-device measurements are available through the worker monitor.
+- **D:** `dynamo-collect/dynamo-sweep/dynamo-merge`, worker `beam_tools_sample`:
+  first-30-second historical sample windows (last sample before cutoff), optional
+  explicit linear/whole-window modes, full offered-TPS/layout/clock/length sweep,
+  unique-device validation and sorted CSV merge. Duplicate-key averaging requires
+  explicit selection. No reinterpretation of `gpu_power` as energy/request.
+  Export/collection/sweep/merge enforce native-compatible positive integer
+  clock/TP/PP/TPS, strictly positive required power/latencies, and nonnegative std.
+- **F:** `beam_tools.py evaluate/fidelity_metrics/fidelity_svg`: request-local
+  MAE/bias/MAPE, missing pairs, explicit token/direct/artifact-shift alignment,
+  TTFT scatter SVG, plus `visualize/compare/heatmap`: Pareto nondomination with
+  min/max objectives/ties/optional artifact filters; latency-versus-energy/power
+  panels; sampled energy/clock, host-enqueue/CUDA-duration, S1/S2/KV/connector and
+  algorithm timing timelines; system/Dynamo profile heatmaps. These are new
+  stdlib SVG readers preserving metrics, not historical plotting-module imports.
+  Multi-run comparisons also require manifest/result model, endpoint, tokenizer,
+  sampling and energy-window/monitor/control-wait cohort identity. Intended mode
+  and TP/PP differences remain allowed; incomparable settings raise diagnostics.
+- **O:** `overhead` times actual target S1/S1-DVFS/S2/TPOT pure selectors with a
+  synthetic or explicit profile; `clock-overhead` measures worker actuation and
+  HTTP/RPC separately, with real initial-state transitions and finally reset.
+- **G:** ServeGen exact regeneration blocked: pinned tree contains 43 dataset
+  JSONs, **no required `chunk-N-trace.csv` files**; `clientpool.py:139–182`
+  requires those. Its PDF `eval` loader and generator duration/default mismatch
+  need separate adaptation. Existing five timestamp CSVs work through R.
+- **H:** Original `deprecated/` entrypoints remain archival, as labeled by the
+  artifact itself. Their relevant metric families are superseded by P/D/F/O;
+  old simulators are not authoritative models of the new PP retirement contract.
+  Owned exact-coordinate mixed observations are now available through P. Legacy
+  per-forward energy equivalence is not inferred from host counter windows; true
+  GPU-completion timelines still require external clock-correlation traces.
+  No old script is labeled unchanged-target-runnable.
