+## 7. Measurement denominators, margins and calibration gate
+
+Record the acceptance thresholds **before** comparing runs; no numeric performance/energy improvement or SLO margin is established in this task.
+
+- Worker `elapsed_time`: relative CUDA-event **ms** around actual model forward; excludes sampling and is not end-to-end/PP wall latency. `batch_size` is padded forward tokens; `num_scheduled_tokens` is unpadded scheduled work. Keep both counts and rank coverage.
+- Energy: `(final_stop_total_energy_mj - start_total_energy_mj)/1000` gives Joules for that **physical-device profile window**. Duration is a positive monotonic stop-start interval; average Watts is Joules/seconds. Never sum cumulative enqueue `curr_energy`, divide it by tokens, or label it isolated forward energy. Rank windows are staggered; aggregate only unique physical UUIDs, acknowledging host/idle/other-device activity and instrumentation.
+- Owned mixed `actual_forward_count=1` is one logical pipeline batch, not sum of rank kernels. Decode context sum includes each query and excludes the prefill prompt; validate observed coordinates and worker CSVs before averaging. Schema is `beam_owned_mixed_window_v1`, `energy_label=window_amortized_not_legacy_per_forward`, `legacy_lookup_compatible=false`, `calibration_claim=false`. No automatic EnergySimulator export or numeric equivalence is provided.
+- Dynamo `gpu_power` is Watts; latency fields/SLO lookup use ms. Offered TPS is positive integer input-token rate, not requests/s or observed output throughput. Historical power uses the last actual counter sample at/before the first-30-second cutoff with complete coverage; linear/whole-window alternatives must be explicit. `ClockChoice.energy_per_req_j` is a historical field name, not a unit reinterpretation.
+- Client TTFT/ITL exclude separate client queue time; E2EL ends at last token-bearing frame. Nonempty native token-ID deltas count empty-decoded terminal tokens; role/usage/empty-ID metadata do not count. `benchmark_script.metrics:317–354` adds TPOT to its distribution only for known output length >1, dividing `(latency-TTFT)` by `(length-1)`; single-token requests use zero only for the no-intertoken-phase goodput predicate, not as a measured TPOT sample. Unknown counts are excluded from that predicate and make aggregate output-throughput/goodput unknown. Chunk ITL with grouped IDs is not per-token latency. Throughput duration must be positive; unknown counts remain null, not zero.
+- Fidelity token alignment requires complete token-ID coverage and matching request-local output/chunk/estimate counts; skip first-token estimate for ITLs. Grouped/text-only streams require explicit direct/artifact-shift frame alignment or exclusion. Never flatten across requests. Report missing/failed/unpaired counts and MAE/bias/MAPE, including null when no pair exists.
+- Cohorts must match model/revision, tokenizer/endpoint/template, exact saved workload/arrivals, sampling, monitor/window/tail and control-wait policy; intended mode/TP/PP differences may vary only with valid profiles. Preserve warmup/measurement boundaries and repeat comparable windows. Declare timing/energy noise tolerance, SLO headroom and counter resolution adequate for the denominator; measure them rather than asserting historical margins. Check monitor RPC perturbation, client saturation and O(forwards) event memory with bounded windows.
+
+**Calibration gate:** old profile rows are not validated by successful parsing, and new owned windows are not old per-forward rows. Review model/GPU/TP/PP/runner/backend/numeric domain, collect matched measurements, quantify prediction error and define justified margins before trusting automatic feasibility. Runtime calibration is a later evidence task, not a missing implementation API or a development blocker hidden as “pending port.”
