+## Source contracts that permit the bounded route
+
+| Contract | Exact source evidence | Consequence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Global layer names survive native PP partitioning | `vllm/model_executor/models/utils.py:632-664`: `make_layers` obtains native start/end indices, uses missing-layer placeholders, and constructs real layers with `prefix=f"{prefix}.{idx}"` for global `idx`. `vllm/model_executor/models/llama.py:378-382` uses this API. | An unambiguous global layer index can identify the destination PP interval. Registration additionally requires exactly one actual KV layer for every index in the local native interval; local renumbering, gaps, and ambiguous/multiple indices fail. |
+| Native partitions are not necessarily equal | `vllm/distributed/utils.py:109-154` reads `VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION` or computes an uneven partition. `vllm/config/model.py:1307-1324` uses that API for model-layer intervals. | Read the actual local partition using this API. Require an explicit remote partition and confirm it against the peer's actual partition. Never infer remote ownership by dividing total layers by remote PP size or by reading the local partition environment as remote configuration. |
