+## Advertised bounded mode and invariants
+
+The core policy candidate is opt-in NVIDIA CUDA text-decoder generation using the verified GPU worker, native scheduler, chunked prefill and an explicitly selected profile. The seven preserved mode fields are `custom_profiler`, `use_s1`, `use_s1_dvfs_only`, `use_s2`, `use_window_based_dvfs_only`, `measure_fidelity` and `disagg_mode`; profiler-only operation does not require a policy lookup profile. Default-disabled paths leave BEAM policy/clock intent absent. Profiles do not model speculation, context parallelism, encoder/multimodal work or aligned Mamba chunks. Distributed external-launcher S1/S2 and legacy-Ray policy execution are rejected; RayV2 selects the real worker execution path. Owned mixed profiling and P2P have **additional**, different restrictions, not a blanket promise for every core-admitted configuration.
+
+**SAFETY — scheduler ownership:** native allocation, preemption, prefix caching, blocked/skipped queues, encoder accounting, maximum-token guards, structured output and `_update_after_schedule` remain authoritative. BEAM changes admission before allocation and attaches finalized telemetry afterward. Never resize the executor queue, reset absolute decode eligibility, or retire sampling merely on abort/Future readiness.
+
+**SAFETY — PP:** the period is physical P, not selected m. An effective m change dispatches exactly P real zero-work invocations, then drains old FIFO/deferred sampling without refill before owner remap. V2 applies carried samples even on an empty invocation. A request ID with an unretired sampling invocation cannot be reused for new sampling. This can miss owner phases and change latency/energy relative to the artifact heuristic. Local conditional progress arguments and 15 scenarios are in [BEAM_TEST_PLAN.md](BEAM_TEST_PLAN.md); they are not a proof of global deadlock freedom.
+
+**SAFETY — hardware and measurement:** only assigned workers initialize NVML or actuate clocks. Stop-time counter windows are physical-device energy; relative CUDA-event forward duration is neither per-forward energy attribution nor an absolute GPU timeline. No legacy lookup calibration is automatically exported from owned windows.
+
