+## Runtime controls: complete source chain and semantics
+
+| HTTP route | Typed request / units | Actual consumer / success response |
+|---|---|---|
+| POST `/update_ttft_slo` | `UpdateTtftSloRequest`, `ttft_slo`: positive finite numeric seconds, no bool/string coercion | S1 or window baseline; `BeamScheduler.update_slo`; HTTP 200 empty body |
+| POST `/update_tbt_slo` | `UpdateTbtSloRequest`, `tbt_slo`: same seconds domain | TBT-S1 except producer disagg exemption, S2, or window baseline; HTTP 200 empty body |
+| POST `/update_tpot_slo` | `UpdateTpotSloRequest`, `tpot_slo`: same seconds domain | S1 with `beam_s1_policy="tpot"` only; HTTP 200 empty body |
+| POST `/update_chunk_size` | `UpdateChunkSizeRequest`: positive strict int `chunk_size` **or** `{"clear":true}`, never both/empty; extra fields forbidden | Enabled BEAM helper, including profiler-only cap; bounded by actual configured scheduled-token hard ceiling; DVFS-only accepts numeric 256 only; JSON queued/applied snapshot |
+| POST `/update_microbatch_size` | `UpdateMicrobatchSizeRequest`: positive strict int `microbatch_size` **or** clear; upper bound physical P | S2 only; persistent requested m, clock optimization at fixed m; JSON queued/applied snapshot |
+| GET `/beam_status` | No mutation or policy evaluation | Enabled local helper or DP envelope; requested/effective/manual/pending, physical P/state/flush/invocations/cohorts and owned-profile diagnostic when relevant |
+
+1. `attach_router` exposes controls even with BEAM disabled so the failure is explicit. Native `AuthenticationMiddleware` adds these six root paths to its configured-key guard alongside existing inference prefixes; mounted/root paths are normalized. Missing/wrong configured key fails before state change. No configured key preserves native open-server behavior; do not confuse that with harness all-route authentication.
+2. HTTP methods call `AsyncLLM.update_*` / `get_beam_status`, which forward to async core-client methods. Sync `LLMEngine` and Inproc/SyncMPClient expose corresponding methods; public `LLM` adds manual controls/status and compatible profiling. Clients validate before transport; Core validates again before a helper mutation. Unsupported consumers raise, never accepted no-ops. Body and policy errors return validation/400 errors; transport/runtime failures do not become a successful empty 200.
+3. MP calls use `call_utility`/`call_utility_async`, native utility serialization and `_process_utility_output`. Core utility lookup/argument conversion executes the actual update. Inproc forwards directly to the same Core. Scheduler `update_slo` updates its active values/config, Dynamo ms fields where applicable and dirty S2 decision state.
+4. DP `DPLBAsyncMPClient.call_utility_async` gathers calls on every core. Manual controls/status return `{"status":...,"engines":[...]}`; SLO fan-out retains the native first-result success convention after gather. **This is nontransactional**: a remote failure can occur after another replica has mutated. There is no cross-engine rollback/atomic effective boundary. Inspect every engine and retry/reconcile explicitly after failure.
+5. Manual chunk intent is snapshotted at `begin_step`, never changes already queued outputs, persists until new command/clear/restart and caps local admission. A supported profiled size may be outside the automatic candidate catalog. An unprofiled size uses safe progress/high clock with model-unavailable metadata rather than invented estimates. Effective is a ceiling, not actual emitted tokens.
+6. Manual m persists across cohort/SLO changes, but prefill temporarily supersedes it with P. Changes use the full fixed flush/retire/remap protocol. `clear` returns to automatic selection, not a queue resize. Requested, pending, effective and prefill-superseded state must be distinguished. `backend_request_func.wait_for_beam_control:120–161` waits on **all** engine states or times out; it never treats a queued ACK as applied.
+
+## SAFETY notes and limits of inference
+
+- **Native state is authoritative.** Admission precedes KV allocation; only finalized actual work is annotated. PP sampling owners, engine Futures and worker sample carry are distinct lifetimes. See the 15 PP scenarios and conditional progress argument in the test plan; no global deadlock-free proof is claimed.
+- **Unsafe raw storage invariant.** Pool `ctypes.from_address`/`torch.frombuffer` views borrow a live buddy reservation. Opt-in engine lock must span descriptor lookup/load/free and complete copies. `on_reserve` transfers rollback ownership before any view/copy; publication transfers that ownership onward. On unconfirmed stream sync, retain raw address and source tensor; do not free/reuse merely because the request finished. Quarantine is containment, not recovery.
+- **Failed reply ownership is terminal for progress.** A failed collective/partial response may leave stale replies. Owned-trial cleanup must not issue later worker RPCs on that stream. Public Core collective/dummy/deferred dispatch guards and utility dispatcher enforce restart-required containment; diagnostic reads do not establish device quiescence.
+- **Measurement is domain-specific.** CUDA-event ms covers actual model forward, not sampling/end-to-end latency. Cumulative mJ at enqueue end is not per-forward energy. Use final start/stop window counters for Joules. Absolute GPU timeline reconstruction requires external GPU/host clock correlation; labels must stay host-enqueue/CUDA-duration.
+- **Final source conclusion:** complete candidate for the matrix's bounded contract. No automated validation, runtime/calibration result, full artifact reproduction, general asymmetric disaggregation, production readiness or distribution clearance is established by this record.
