+| 8 | Decrease m under load | Exactly P real zero-work dispatches, then finite FIFO retirement without refill, only then remap | engine physical-flush test |
+| 9 | Increase m / clear / coalesced commands | Same fixed flush, latest intent at drained boundary; queue capacity/absolute step unchanged | manual m / SLO-arrival coalescing tests |
+| 10 | Last-request completion | Offline/Inproc/DP predicates keep maintenance awake until both ownership domains drain | pipeline offline-loop + API DP-consensus tests |
+| 11 | Cancellation / ID reuse | Owner invalidated, pending sampling retained until matching retire; late output cannot mutate replacement/incarnation | scheduler late abort/reuse/streaming tests |
+| 12 | KV pressure / preemption / failed load | Native allocation remains authoritative; invalidating ownership never releases in-flight guard | KV pressure/preempt/invalid-block tests |
+| 13 | Empty maintenance invocation | Reaches workers; V2 applies previous samples before zero-token return, no fake forward | V2 `execute_model:1092–1103`, `PPHandler` |
+| 14 | Async/deferred/out-of-order result | FIFO update/retirement; already dispatched structured sampling completes in RETIRE_ONLY; no new refill | pipeline deferred/FIFO tests |
+| 15 | New prefill or SLO/manual change during drain | Flush not restarted; prefill temporarily forces P; persistent manual m restored through another safe boundary after prefill | manual m / coalescing / streaming-prefill-stop tests |
+
+### Local conditional progress argument, not global deadlock freedom
+
+1. `begin_step` starts FLUSH only from ACTIVE and initializes `flush_remaining=P`; `finalize` decrements it once per **actually dispatched** empty output. Dirty changes during FLUSH do not restart the count.
+2. At zero, RETIRE_ONLY forbids new scheduler dispatch/refill. Old FIFO and already deferred sampling still retire in native order. Request identity guards release only in `retire` after native output handling, not on Future readiness/abort.
+3. Owner remap requires both empty engine FIFO/no deferred entry and no outstanding helper invocations. The V2 worker ring is a distinct domain: P real empties advance its T+P carry before remapping, without modifying ring capacity.
+4. BEAM maintenance predicates keep offline/DP loops awake after public requests vanish. P and native queue capacity remain fixed; absolute `current_step` and upstream eligibility are not reset.
+
+**Conditional on upstream execute/sample/Futures/collectives completing and the engine continuing to step**, this gives a finite local flush/drain boundary. It does not prove progress under NCCL/socket failure, scheduling starvation, failed worker teardown, unsupported placement or every concurrent arrival pattern. Owned-profile ambiguous streams quarantine instead of attempting an unbounded drain. Later hardware timeouts and independent peer/clock observations are mandatory.
+
+## Execution order and acceptance record
+
+Use the later-only commands and environment in [BEAM_DEPLOYMENT_VALIDATION.md](BEAM_DEPLOYMENT_VALIDATION.md). Order: dependency/provenance preparation → model/config → scheduler/pipeline → API/fidelity → DVFS/profiler → owned-profile/P2P/tools source tests → vanilla GPU smoke → bounded policies/controls → failure/restoration → matched profiling/calibration → P2P deployment. Record collection failures separately from assertion/runtime failures; neither can be described as “no tests needed.” No coverage percentage, passing count or hardware result is supplied by this plan.
