+### Burst, stair, Pareto and ordered campaign sequencing
+
+`--rates` generates gamma-distributed arrivals with seeded stdlib RNG and
+rate-weighted phase request counts. It preserves the algorithm family, not
+NumPy's exact random stream or the artifact's round-and-adjust tie behavior.
+`requests.json` records actual prompts/arrivals, making the difference explicit.
+Phase records include `end_time`; rate charts use horizontal start/end segments
+and duplicate each transition x-coordinate with old/new rates, including the
+final phase end. They depict steps, not interpolated ramps.
+Use `--requests /absolute/earlier-run/requests.json` instead of `--trace`/`--rates`
+to replay those exact inputs across baseline modes without regenerating prompts.
+
+| Legacy workflow | Arguments/cases to `run` or `campaign` |
+|---|---|
+| e2e | A, B2, D; same `--trace`, model, TP/PP, SLOs |
+| ablation | A, B3, C, D as actually called by legacy main; B/B2 also supported explicitly; `--rates 4 --num-prompts 180 --input-len 512 --output-len 64 --range-ratio .5` |
+| burst | A, B2, D; `--rates 4 4 20 4 4 --num-prompts 1000 --input-len 256 --output-len 64 --range-ratio .5` |
+| stair | A, B2, D; `--rates 2 2.4 2.8 3.2 3.6 4 4.4 4.8 5.2 5.6 6 6.4 --num-prompts 2000 --input-len 1000 --output-len 64 --range-ratio .5` |
+| fidelity | D `--fidelity --rates 8 --num-prompts 400 --input-len 300 --output-len 100 --range-ratio .8` |
+| Pareto | D; TP4/PP2 and TP2/PP4; each TBT `.06 .10 .14 .18 .22`, TTFT `1`; `--rates 1 --num-prompts 60 --input-len 1024 --output-len 64 --range-ratio .4`; explicit matching profile per layout |
