+## Remaining contracts for the orchestrator
+
+| Boundary | Exact source evidence and required next contract |
+|---|---|
+| Fixed-clock B and monitoring | Implemented in `worker_tools.py`: `beam_tools_identity()`, `beam_tools_clock(request: str)`, `beam_tools_sample()`. Load through native `worker_extension_cls` and the supplied authenticated middleware. No additional core worker method is pending for these operations. |
+| Owned mixed profiling | Implemented: `mixed-profile` consumes `EngineCore.beam_profile_trial` via SyncMP utility or direct Inproc ownership, records exact observations/worker windows and skips mismatches. The native schema intentionally remains non-legacy and uncalibrated; no profiling API implementation is pending here. |
+| Live chunk/microbatch controls | Implemented target POST/GET APIs are consumed by typed clients and optional harness scalar/clear/pattern flags. Each command retains its acknowledgment and polls all engine states until effective or explicit timeout; physical P/queue ownership stay with the core. |
+| ServeGen regeneration | Required `chunk-N-trace.csv` rate/CV/pattern inputs are absent from the pinned tree; loader `clientpool.py:139–182` requires them. Existing request CSV replay is implemented. |
+| True GPU kernel completion timeline | Worker CSVs contain host enqueue wall time plus relative CUDA-event duration, not GPU start/end timestamps correlated to the host clock. Kernel timelines require an actual GPU correlation trace. Current SVGs explicitly separate enqueue time and CUDA duration. |
+
+Only ServeGen source traces and GPU clock-correlation traces are absent external
+inputs for the respective regeneration/kernel-timeline workflows. Owned-window
+numerical calibration and execution-based validation remain unperformed.
+The separate same-TP/asymmetric-PP P2P implementation and its remaining transport
+limits are documented in `BEAM_P2P_COMPATIBILITY.md`, not marked absent tooling.
+This continuation adds no core,
+config, engine, or GPU-worker source changes and creates no commits.
+
+Future operator checks need both runners, TP/PP1/2/4 rank coverage, supported and
